  "volume_definition": "Gross cylinder: pi * OD_mm**2 * overall_length_mm / 4 / 1000; bore included; published envelope held fixed.",
  "method": "At zero electrical angle, screen both endpoints of every listed input separately using total torque at the saved nominal currents. Use those sensitivities to choose combined low/high settings, solve all five original positions, and re-optimize balanced currents at 5.5 W. Bounds are the minimum/maximum sampled five-position mean, including the original nominal mean; not guaranteed global extrema or statistical confidence limits. For the final Kollmorgen bounds, preserve its paired-current driven-torque definition (T(+I)-T(-I))/2.",
  "geometry": "Preserve winding insulation clearance as hidden tooth/yoke/shoe dimensions vary; recompute copper fill from turns, winding dimensions and the published resistance. Keep the TQ winding head inside its dimensioned 47.6 mm OD and both Steadywin windings inside their overall axial envelopes. Extend shape changes through the air with a common affine mesh; rebuild CAD and remesh when the original tetrahedra cannot follow without folding. The CAD reconstruction reproduces each nominal solid to less than 1e-4 mm3 symmetric difference.",
  "material_law": "Scale steel magnetic polarization J=B-mu0*H by 0.95..1.05 and H by 0.8..1.2 independently; add back mu0*H to preserve the vacuum slope. Stator stacking factor varies 0.93..0.97. Ring pole transitions span 0..10% of a pole pitch, represented by the equivalent mean Br reduction in the existing edge slices of each pole.",
  "range_units": "Ranges below are additive deviations from the nominal inputs. br, stator_J, stator_H, rotor_J and rotor_H are fractional changes; mur and stack are absolute changes; *_mm are mm; *_deg are mechanical degrees; turns are turns per tooth; pole_transition is a fraction of pole pitch.",
  "held_fixed": "Published envelope and stator stack lengths, slot/pole counts, connections, phase assignment, terminal resistance, power, temperature, field equations and final zero-floor Newton tolerance 1e-9. Alternate current conventions, different slot counts, lamination anisotropy and unmodeled skew are outside this parameter study.",
  "engineering_ranges": "Engineering estimates around the present reconstruction, not measured production tolerances or fitted catalog torque: hidden core dimensions usually 0.05..0.10 mm, gap 0.03 mm, winding dimensions 0.02..0.03 mm with linked insulation clearances, inferred turns 1..2, sintered Br 5%, bonded Br 10%; Kollmorgen uses its previously declared 1.18..1.32 T grade range and the documented axial mounting tolerance 0.40 mm.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://www.eclipsemagnetics.com/site/assets/files/22177/eclipsemagnetics_ndfeb_datasheet.pdf",
      "use": "Manufacturer guidance: typical magnet dimensional tolerances 0.05..0.10 mm; grade-dependent remanence. Reconstruction uncertainty need not equal a production tolerance."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.arnoldmagnetics.com/products/neodymium-iron-boron-magnets/",
      "use": "Sintered NdFeB grade families and nominal remanence."
    },
